  "description": "Single storey rear extension. \n• Maximum rear projection of 4m from the rear of the house.\n• Maximum height of 3.85m measured from garden level.\n• Retention of the side access path, maintaining separation from the boundary with No. 29. \n• Brickwork to match the existing house to preserve visual coherence. \n• Flat roof with parapet and coping stone.\n• Slimline, thermally broken aluminium sliding doors opening to the rear garden. \n• A slender rooflight set along the junction with the existing rear elevation to maximise \ndaylight and provide opening sections for summer ventilation. \n• The Ground floor level is currently raised by 530mm over the back garden level and it will \nbe kept as existing following the flood risk reports recommendations.",
